# A backstop, not the release path.
#
# Releases build images through goreleaser, which assembles its own context in a
# temp directory holding just the Dockerfile and the cross-compiled binaries —
# this file is not consulted there at all. It exists because the Dockerfile sits
# at the repository root, so `docker build .` is the obvious thing to try, and
# the previous Dockerfile did exactly that with `COPY . .` and no .dockerignore:
# a 731MB context carrying .env — the real ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY, JWT_SECRET,
# database password and Proxmox token — plus .dragon-buddy/ and docs/security/.
# The final stage copied only the binary, but layers are extractable, so anything
# pushed to a registry shipped those credentials.
#
# The current Dockerfile copies two named binaries and nothing else, so no
# context can leak through it. This stays so that a future `COPY .` cannot
# reintroduce the problem silently.

# Credentials and local-only notes. Never in an image, under any Dockerfile.
.env
.env.*
.dragon-buddy/
docs/security/

# Nothing here belongs in an image, and it is what made the context 731MB.
.git/
**/node_modules/
**/.yarn/
bin/
dist/
repomix-output.md
